h you know how can we not take a look  at what's happening in our very own  country you know just it's a human  crisis  like it's not just like oh it's  immigration it's really about it's  humanity how are we choosing to treat  people  you know and and that is everyone's  responsibility  so you can't just sit back idle and do  nothing about it  you have to take action on some level  because it's  where unified  be like you know  unified countries like you know it feels  so divided but like you know if if we're  going to call ourselves the united  states and the land of the free then we  actively as residents  we need to  do something to help everyone feel safe  on some level you know and um  i really truly believe when i first saw  this you know a rough rough cut of the  documentary  i immediately wanted to get in my car  and drive to the south of the border and  be like what the hell is going on and  protest and try to help and be of  service  so i i really am  hoping that the people who watch this  film  are also inspired to do something about  it and that that is the point of really  you know shining a light on these  stories and putting them out there for  the world to see  yeah and and to me  everything you said  um and also like  i think people believe they know the  story  but when you put human um  faces and experiences to that story  um  it it  you know whether you take action or not  i hope that you look at women like jenny  and rosie and you're like they should be  in this country  you know they are the kind of citizens  that we have  we have  you know built this country  with and together with and um they are  incredibly important to the to the  future of our country and the fact that  we treat asylum seekers like criminals  when  i hope i'm getting this right i didn't  know that i'm trying to cross the border  for asylum is a misdemeanor  um it's and they're treated like  you know um drug cartel members i mean  it's it's unbelievable so  if only to have more compassion for  people you don't necessarily you think  you understand but you don't  and also to see where these people come  from and the the  the fact that they in many cases are  making life and death decisions for  themselves and their children  again i think sometimes we we you know  all of us sort of think we understand  but we don't um so for me it's always  about empathy it's the same thing i i  focus on in my work like i think empathy  creates action or it should  um you know and in in some cases the  action is just  kindness and i this is reductive but i  was so moved by the kindness of of all  the people involved in this and the  humanness um so even a reminder just to  not make assumptions about people to not  look at their stories and think you know  so  and and again like it's just a very  moving story and it's hopeful  um that's the part that was so difficult  i think and why i wanted to get involved  because you feel so powerless  and you feel like there's nobody  that will do the right thing um and then  you watch this movie and you're like i'm  you know if only i send money to ift  or you know or i support organizations  that i i'll say this one last thing  people need to do their homework about  where they send their money  um and people need to really understand  the impact of these organizations um you  know  no disrespect to the organization that i  helped raise money for but they they  basically provide the bond and what we  learned in our movie is that it takes so  much more than that um to actually help  these people stay here reunite their  families um and and so again you know  it's just looking at things through a  more um focused lens and um and i think  the movie's so successful at that i also  think it's yeah it is hopeful and it's  also really emotional it made me it made  me believe in people again  the hopeful nature of it was very  inspiring to answer my own last question  it's it's like that's that's why i i  think i need a documentary like this in  addition to the information that i get  via news is because often news lacks  that hope or  lacks that uh the ability to point you  in the direction to actually take action  on your own whereas this movie provides  the hope to inspire you to do it and  even gives you the proper information in  order to make those smart decisions when  you want to support a cause  i must let you go  thank you for your time today  congratulations on the film i am very  eager to see it get out there even  further beyond south by southwest thank  you all right thank you so much
 

